function filterDiffPathOf(params, ticketKey) {
   // The review leg's diff: the first input-folder candidate that actually
   // holds pr_diff.txt. The chain is ticketKeyShapes.inputFolderCandidates
   // (gh-1403 review thread 1): params.inputFolderPath when the dispatch
   // carries it (unwrapping the jobParams wrapper, linkedIssuesReport
   // shape), else the Java-derived input/<inputFolderNameFor(key)> layout —
   // a composite key owner/repo#1407 dispatches input/gh-1407, not
   // input/<raw key> — then the legacy input/<ticketKey>. When no candidate
   // holds the file the first candidate is named anyway: fail-open, the
   // same degradation class as every other filter failure.
   var actualParams = params && params.inputFolderPath ? params : ((params && params.jobParams) || params || {});
   var folders = ticketKeyShapes.inputFolderCandidates(actualParams.inputFolderPath, ticketKey);
   for (var i = 0; i < folders.length; i++) {
       if (readInputFileOrNull(folders[i] + '/pr_diff.txt')) return folders[i] + '/pr_diff.txt';
   }
   return folders[0] + '/pr_diff.txt';
}
``

Check: `readInputFileOrNull` is defined at ~line 1990 (function declaration → hoisted; module top-level function declarations are available). Fine.

Edge: params null → actualParams = {} → folders from (undefined, key) — inputFolderCandidates handles null explicit. folders[0] always exists ('input/' + name or 'input/undefined' degenerate) — never crashes.

**Fix B** — isCommentFilePath helper + guard:
Add near resolveCommentFileReference:
```javascript
var COMMENT_FILE_PATH_RE = /^(outputs\/)?(pr_review_comments\/)?[\w.\-]+\.md$/;

/**
 * The one model-written-path guard (gh-1350 class): a .md file reference is
 * only trusted in the comment-file layout — bare name, pr_review_comments/
 * or outputs/ prefixed. Every read AND write of a model-written file
 * reference goes through this shape check (gh-1403 review thread 2: the
 * demote stamp wrote `entry.comment` unguarded — a hallucinated path could
 * append to any readable file relative to the runtime cwd).
 */
function isCommentFilePath(value) {
   return typeof value === 'string' && COMMENT_FILE_PATH_RE.test(value.trim());
}
``
- resolveCommentFileReference: replace the inline regex check with `if (!isCommentFilePath(value)) return null;`
- filterPathOfGeneralComment: `if (!path || !isCommentFilePath(path)) return null;`
